{"type":"text","timestamp":1792556217013,"sessionID":"ses_ea354b611ffeumCv81W7kKu2YE","part":{"id":"prt_15cacb33a001gxsxFGyZmRF3cO","messageID":"msg_15cac7450001euDJSbZcOpTR8l","sessionID":"ses_ea354b611ffeumCv81W7kKu2YE","type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p1:step\",\n      \"status\": \"UNREACHABLE\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Source is a PDF; the fetcher returned raw PDF binary (compressed FlateDecode streams) and no page text could be extracted, so the recorded quote ('The predictive power of in vitro receptor binding is confirmed by AAV transduction in cell lines with receptor expression') could not be located or checked on the page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p1:activity\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"THOUSAND OAKS, Calif., May 12, 2026 — Capsida Biotherapeutics, (“Capsida”) a next-generation genetic medicines company, today provided corporate and pipeline updates related to its ocular and central nervous system (CNS) programs.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim; page dated May 12, 2026, reports ASGCT 2026 presentations (meeting May 11-15, 2026), CNS updates including ongoing ADAM15/CAP-002 interaction experiments and a next-generation capsid using receptor RECK ('Capsida is moving forward development of a next-generation capsid, which uses a distinct receptor, RECK, to cross the BBB').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p1:c1\",\n      \"status\": \"UNREACHABLE\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Same PDF source; content returned as unreadable binary, so the quote about patent filings for the five novel receptors ('Capsida Biotherapeutics has successfully filed patents for all five of these groundbreaking novel receptors...') could not be verified on the page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p1:c2\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"At Capsida, the scale at which we have engineered capsids is unrivaled. Using our automated, high-throughput biological screening, our scientists assess large, diverse engineered capsid libraries for CNS and the eye in models relevant to humans to quickly identify optimal capsids that target tissues and cells in organs of interest.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim on the Science & Innovation page and directly supports the scale/automation/people claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p1:c3\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"The ongoing experiments include studying the interaction between the engineered viral capsid contained in CAP-002 and the ADAM15 protein, its primary receptor for crossing the blood brain barrier (BBB). Based on the learning over the past six months, Capsida believes that the receptor is a key factor in designing CNS gene therapy.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim; RECK claim also on page ('moving forward development of a next-generation capsid, which uses a distinct receptor, RECK').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p1:done\",\n      \"status\": \"UNREACHABLE\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Same PDF source; unreadable binary on fetch, so neither the recorded quote nor the absence of any public record of computed pose enumeration could be checked from the page text.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p2:step\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Owing to its structural homogeneity, modelling the complete 60-mer AAV capsid is usually unnecessary, but portions of the surface such as at the 2, 3 and 5-fold axes are the minimum subunit for useful docking or structural assessment of capsid stability in silico.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim on the Lir Starfish blog; page also links Starfish surface generation to receptor docking screens and nAAVigator/lab-in-the-loop, supporting the step description.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p2:activity\",\n      \"status\": \"UNREACHABLE\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"The VectorBuilder newsroom page is a JavaScript-rendered app ('Loading... Please Wait'); the news content did not load in the fetched text and the recorded quote about the Lir Therapeutics collaboration does not appear on the page as fetched, so the August 18, 2026 announcement claim could not be checked.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p2:c1\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Our method scales far better than multimer cofolding both in terms of runtime and compute requirements, with Starfish™ able to assemble the full capsid at acceptable runtimes for screening tens of thousands of variants.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim; page also states 'The first stage of our pipeline involves applying a protein folding model to generate the monomers ... followed by fast physics-based assembly and refinement algorithms' and Starfish 'using cost-efficient hardware'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p2:c2\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"We first showcased an application of this technology at ESGCT 2025 in Seville, demonstrating that screening of the LY6A receptor was possible by performing docking to variant capsid surfaces constructed using Starfish™. We found a structural approach identified an alternative subset of hits compared to a language model-based approach, with the two methods being additive.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim; 'We've been using this same approach for other receptors to investigate experimental targets predicted to exhibit differential binding' supports the 'then other receptors' claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p2:c3\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"We've found larger docking surfaces have been required to get relevant docking scores for screening purposes. ... All approaches generate the 3-fold axes of AAV9 wild-type with an RMSD <1Å\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim; RMSD <1 Å for AAV9 3-fold axes appears on the page, and page describes tuning by docking-surface size (no run-count tuning is mentioned).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p2:done\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"We first showcased an application of this technology at ESGCT 2025 in Seville, demonstrating that screening of the LY6A receptor was possible by performing docking to variant capsid surfaces constructed using Starfish™.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim; the page contains no published bind/no-bind accuracy against a labelled capsid-by-receptor grid and no 54-to-432 run-count scaling test, consistent with the card's negative claims.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p3:step\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Automated Pair-wise Peptide-Receptor binding model AnalysIs for Screening Engineered proteins (APPRAISE) is a method that predicts the receptor binding propensity of engineered proteins based on high-precision protein structure prediction tools, such as AlphaFold2-multimer.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim in the APPRAISE GitHub README; repo is 'Rank binders by structure modeling', references the Ding/Gradinaru Molecular Therapy 2024 manuscript (with Shay as co-author), and the demo uses AAV peptides (PHP.eB, AAV9) vs receptors such as LY6A, supporting the computed capsid–receptor binding-call step.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p3:activity\",\n      \"status\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Former CLOVER Research Scientists and Gradinaru lab alumns Xiaozhe Ding and Xinhong Chen led a multidisciplinary effort ... that generated a small molecule shuttle to efficiently deliver biological cargo across the blood-brain barrier (BBB) of mice and non-human primates. ... catch the full story in Nature Chemical Biology.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim on the CLOVER news page dated August 27, 2026, and supports the Nature Chemical Biology CA-IV shuttle paper. However, the item's additional claim of a March 30, 2026 Molecular Therapy paper on AAV9-X1.1/CAP-B10 structure characterization is not on this page and has no source checked.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p3:c1\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"After generating structural models of engineered proteins competing for binding to a target using an established structure prediction tool such as AlphaFold-Multimer or ESMFold, APPRAISE performs a rapid (under 1 CPU second per model) scoring analysis that takes into account biophysical and geometrical constraints.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim in the CaltechAUTHORS abstract; supports the under-1-CPU-second physics/geometry-informed scoring claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p3:c2\",\n      \"status\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles, predict selective interaction with human LRP6 domain E1 (E1 and E2: teal, E3 and E4: yellow, AAV peptides: purple).\",\n      \"note\": \"The 5-model/20-recycle AlphaFold prediction and the SPR LRP6-E1E2-vs-E3E4 labels ('SPR of mouse LRP6-E1E2 and LRP6-E3E4 ... confirms that AAV9-X1.1 and CAP-Mac bind only to LRP6-E1E2') are supported on the Shay et al. PMC page, but the 'on one A100 GPU' compute detail does not appear in the fetched page text, so it is unverified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p3:c3\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"using a combination of biophysical techniques including cryo-ET sub-tomogram averaging with symmetry expansion, we were able to locate the human IL3 binding site on the side of AAV9’s threefold symmetry spike adjacent to the capsid’s twofold symmetry valley and generate an integrative binding model.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim in the paper's discussion; the IL3 cryo-ET site on the threefold spike and the integrative computed model are both on the page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"p3:done\",\n      \"status\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"As proof-of-concept cases, we demonstrate that APPRAISE can accurately classify receptor-dependent vs. receptor-independent adeno-associated viral vectors and diverse classes of engineered proteins such as miniproteins targeting the severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) spike, nanobodies targeting a G-protein-coupled receptor, and peptides that specifically bind to transferrin receptor or programmed death-ligand 1 (PD-L1).\",\n      \"note\": \"The proof-of-concept classification claim is verbatim in the CaltechAUTHORS abstract and supports part of the item. The Shay-2024 detail (5-model AlphaFold-Multimer LRP6 predictions scored against SPR bind/no-bind labels for ~six capsids) is only partly supported from the cited source — it requires the companion PMC page; also on that paper the cryo-ET site-localization was done for human IL3 on AAV9, not for the LRP6-domain predictions, so the claimed joint SPR+cryo-ET scoring of the LRP6 predictions is not confirmed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","time":{"start":1792556184379,"end":1792556217006}}}
